SEM was adopted to specify the surface topography of the HA-DNA hydrogel-coated MOFzyme (Fig. 3D). A hydrogel coating was deposited on the surface of the MOFzyme. Additionally, the formation of hydrogels did not substantially lead to the agglomeration of MOFzyme, which would be beneficial for the practical application of the developed aptasensor. Overall, an ideal HA-DNA hydrogel coating was successfully deposited on the surface of oxidized bimetallic MOFzyme via the HCR reaction initiated by the promoter unit in nucleotide (2).
3.6 Feasibility
